### Theme switcher (Equalize tokens + Tailwind)

- Import `equalize-theme-templates.css` **before** Tailwind; Tailwind `@layer base { body { background-color: var(--color-background) } }` **overrides** `body { background: var(--bg) }` — themes appear broken (always white/light).
- **Fix:** after Tailwind base, force embed shells:
  ```css
  html[class$="-embed"],
  html[class$="-embed"] body {
    background-color: var(--bg) !important;
    color: var(--txt-hi) !important;
  }
  ```
- **`useGameTheme`:** always `document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', theme)` — do not remove the attribute for midnight.
- Game shells and canvas wrappers: **`var(--bg)` / `var(--txt-hi)`**, not hardcoded `#0A0A0F`, `bg-black`, etc. Theme button needs `pointer-events: auto` and high z-index in iframe.
- **Placement (live audit Jun 2026):** default `ThemeSwitcher` at `bottom: 20px; right: 20px` overlaps bottom trays, modals, and touch zones (confirmed on Pocket Park Tycoon **Reset**, Helicopter Rush play area, Arrow Time arrow-type row). **Hide or relocate** when overlays/menus are open; verify at embed iframe width (~600px), not only full desktop viewport.

### Host site integration (dsapatterns-website) **[applicable if dsapatterns host]**

Vendored static bundles live under `public/games/<slug>/`. The React shell is `src/components/GamesSection.jsx` (hash routes `#games/<slug>`, default `#games/equalize` in `App.jsx`).

#### Outer iframe shell (host)

- **Width:** responsive cap on the games column (`60vw`, `max-w-[900px]`, centered).
- **Height:** stable block so in-iframe CTAs / mode lobbies are not clipped. Host mobile shell often needs **≥ ~960px** effective game height (or `min-h` + `max-h` clamp) — short shells clip Orbit/GRID lobbies and rush home chrome. Prefer `h-[clamp(…)]` / `100dvh` floors; tune per title after screenshot at 390×844.
- **`iframeSrc`:** TanStack CSR embeds use `'/games/<slug>/'` (trailing slash helps SPA entry resolve). Legacy Equalize uses `'/games/equalize/equalize.html'`.

#### Host games page — mobile iframe visibility

- On narrow host viewports (~650px), the games list stacks above the iframe; the embed can start **below the fold** (~1000px+ from top) so users do not see the game after tapping a title.
- **Fix (host):** on `#games/<slug>` change, `scrollIntoView` the iframe region or collapse the nav list on small breakpoints.

#### Tutorial UX inside the iframe (game-side)

- **First-run tutorial** must stay usable when embedded: primary CTAs (**Next**, dots, **Start**) must not sit below a clipped fold.
- **Detect embed early:** `window.self !== window.top` → add compact class on `<html>` as early as possible (inline script right after `<body>` for legacy single-file games; React mount for TanStack titles).
- **Legacy Equalize (`html.eq-embed`):** scale deck (`width: min(96%, 60vw, 720px)`), fluid 3×3 grid (`minmax(0, 1fr)`, `aspect-ratio: 1`), `@media (max-height: 720px)` fallback; `#tut` needs `overflow-y: auto`, `-webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch`, generous `padding-bottom`, and `scroll-padding-bottom` so **Next** stays reachable.
- **TanStack suite:** use `<slug>-embed` on `<html>` plus §12 *Iframe height* layout (`flex-col`, tray above canvas).

#### Adding a vendored game (host checklist)

1. **Upstream:** build with correct Vite `base` + router `basepath` (`/games/<slug>/`); fix or strip manifest / service worker `scope` and `start_url` for embed copy (see Bharat `docs/embed-dsapatterns-puzzles.md`).
2. **Vendor:** copy **client** output only → `public/games/<slug>/` with `index.html` at that root (no SSR bundle required on static host).
3. **`GamesSection.jsx`:** append to `GAMES` with `iframeSrc: '/games/<slug>/'`.
4. **`App.jsx` / `routes.js`:** allow hash route; add `LEGACY_GAME_SLUG_REDIRECTS` if renaming slugs.
5. **Embed CSS:** mirror compact iframe pattern if full-screen UI clips in short iframes.
6. **Hardening:** strip debug globals before commit unless a parallel strip-and-verify pipeline exists (Equalize exception below; TanStack suite → `verify-game-dist-cloudflare.mjs`).
7. **E2E:** add `#games/<slug>` to `e2e/smoke.spec.mjs` `pages` with **stable copy** the test asserts; extend Bharat `campaign-5` when adding a suite title.
8. **README:** note vendored path, sync from upstream (`build-all-embeds.mjs`), honest security copy (client bundles are not secret).

#### Cloudflare vs Vercel (nested SPA client routes)

- `vercel.json` may rewrite `/games/<slug>/*` so deep links (e.g. `/play`) serve the **game** shell, not the marketing SPA.
- **Cloudflare Workers** static hosting uses `wrangler.jsonc` `not_found_handling: single-page-application` for the **main** site — nested game SPAs may still need equivalent routing or path-specific rules; test live deep links after deploy and purge CDN for `/games/*` when hashes look stale.

### Iframe height — critical UI above the fold (game-side)

- Parent iframes are often **~370–500px tall** while a naive `min-h-screen` layout is **700px+**. Trays, CTAs, and instructions below the canvas are **invisible without scroll** (users report “missing mirrors / can’t play”).
- **Fix:** `h-[100dvh] flex flex-col overflow-hidden` on root; **compact header (shrink-0)** → **interactive tray / primary actions (shrink-0, above canvas)** → **playfield (`flex-1 min-h-0`)**.
- Screenshot or Playwright at **embed height**, not only full desktop viewport.

### Touch vs drag (mirror / token trays)

- HTML5 **drag-and-drop does not work reliably on mobile**. If gameplay is “drag from tray,” add **tap-to-select → tap grid cell to place** as the primary mobile path; keep drag as desktop enhancement.
- Label empty tray honestly: puzzle may need **zero tray mirrors** (beam already hits target) — say so in UI, not only in README.

### Level design at scale (20+ levels)

- **Minimum bar:** 20 levels per puzzle game (Echo 30, Laser Mirror 30+); each level named and listed in source.
- **Solvability:** for ray/path puzzles, ship a **solver** (brute-force tray placement + `traceBeam`) and run in CI (`scripts/games/validate-*-puzzles.ts` or test helper). Hand-authored mirror paths must be traced — `/` vs `\` reflection is easy to get wrong.
- **Seeded procedural levels** (e.g. wire grid): `generatePuzzleForLevel(n)` with `LEVEL_COUNT` matching shipped count; clamp level index; verify connected/solvable path for e2e `skipShuffle` builds.
- **Echo / timing games:** e2e uses `?e2e=1` to auto-complete or skip shuffle; `campaign-5` covers levels/waves 1–5 across catalog embeds (and mode URLs for inlined fantasies).

### Audio: `puzzleJuice.ts` (SFX) vs BGM

- **SFX** — `puzzleJuice.ts` per game: WebAudio oscillators, haptics, slow-mo on solve. Call `unlockSfx()` on first user gesture.
- **BGM** — separate from SFX. Two supported paths:
  1. **File BGM** — `HTMLAudioElement` looping files via `scripts/games/templates/bgm.ts` (do not mix into `puzzleJuice.ts`).
  2. **Procedural BGM** — step-sequencer loops via `scripts/games/templates/proceduralMusic/` (`tracks.ts`, `player.ts`) + thin `proceduralBgm.ts` wrapper. Copy into each game's `src/lib/` (never `../../../scripts/` imports). Used when no Suno asset exists (pixel-path `neon`, choppa `boss`, grid-td `dungeon`, parkos `tavern`). Crush the Swappy keeps an 11-track in-game picker (excludes tracks redistributed to embeds).
- **Pilot pattern (file BGM)** — Echo Node reference:
  1. Place loop at `public/audio/<slug>/bgm-loop.{m4a|mp3|ogg}` (Vite copies to `dist/client/`).
  2. Copy `scripts/games/templates/bgm.ts` → `src/lib/bgm.ts`; add thin `gameAudio.ts` wiring `unlockSfx()` + `playBgmLoop()` on first gesture.
  3. Runtime URL: `/games/<slug>/audio/<slug>/bgm-loop.*`
  4. `localStorage` key `<slug>.musicEnabled` (default on; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`).
  5. `duckBgm()` on win overlay; `stopBgm()` on route unmount.
  6. Source tracks live in `games/<folder>/music/` — **do not commit** `music/` folders; only ship `public/audio/` assets. Manifest: `scripts/games/music-asset-manifest.json`; prompts: `docs/game-music-prompts.md`.

### Game-specific pitfalls (verified in production)

| Game | Pitfall | Fix |
|------|---------|-----|
| **Laser / mirror** | Tray below fold; puzzle 1 has 0 mirrors | Tray above canvas; tap-to-place; hint when tray empty |
| **Pixel path** | Player orb only drawn when `running` | Draw orb + gold on title preview and whenever `screen === playing` |
| **Track / urgency** | Random rotation of **path** tiles → instant derail | Scramble **decoys only** when enterable but unsolved; e2e `skipShuffle` + instant win if `isPathConnected` |
| **Echo node** | Doors require plates held while walking to exit | **Latch** doors once both plates pressed together |
| **Neon circuit** | E2E expects win overlay | Pre-solved grid when `?e2e=1`; skip rotation randomization |
| **Theme switcher** | Fixed bottom-right chip overlaps trays/modals | Hide on overlay open or move to header; test ~600px embed width |
| **Host games nav (mobile)** | Iframe below full game list | Scroll embed into view on select or collapse list on `sm:` breakpoints |
| **GhostLoop / embed + skip tutorial** | Start screen hidden but `running` stays false → frozen canvas | On embed mount (not `?e2e=1`), set sim `running = true` when auto-starting past level 1 |
| **Skip early levels** | Returning players stuck on old progress; E2E expects level 1 | Bump `PROGRESS_EPOCH`; floor at `START_LEVEL`; `?e2e=1` bypasses floor; route redirects honor `?e2e=1` |
| **GRID Tower Defense** | Leaks not detected; win on same frame as leak | Pure `creepHasLeaked()` (path end **and** `x >= exit`); `gameOverRef`/`wonRef` in tick; `won = false` on 0 lives |
| **Crush the Swappy / physics ammo** | Bomb only explodes on target hit | Detonate bomb on **any** Matter collision contact; swap launcher ammo when selecting type |
| **Attack the Army / lane TD** | Too many lanes + weak hit feedback | Fewer lanes (e.g. 4) + one `LANES` constant; `damageFlash` vignette + visible miss counter beats more briefing copy |
| **Rename game folder** | Broken embed paths after `git mv` | **Slug stays stable** for CDN/bookmarks; update `embed-registry.mjs`, e2e, `verify-game-dist-cloudflare.mjs`, host `public/games/<slug>/` only |
| **Celebrate / win overlay** | `prefers-reduced-motion` dwell = solve-hold → overlay never paints | Separate `CELEBRATE_VISIBLE_MS` / `solveHoldMs`; never set reduced-motion dwell ≤ hold; `delayMs={0}` on overlay must still allow paint |
| **Rush lobby labels** | Duplicate text (`Survival Survival`) | Secondary line ≠ `MODE_LABELS` (use lives / timed copy) |
| **Audio / SFX dock** | Dock overlaps Modes rail / primary CTA on short mobile | Bottom-right chip + lobby `padding-bottom`; hide when overlays open (same as ThemeSwitcher) |
| **Inlined mode routes** | E2E still hits `/games/orbit-defense/play` | Target flagship mode path; Orbit is often `/modes/orbit/` (GameShell inlined — **no** nested `/play`) |
| **Hard-delete standalone** | Left hub card or vercel rewrite → 404 / zombie SKU | Update together: `embed-registry`, android registry, `GamesSection`, SEO, `GAME_SPA_SLUGS`, `vercel.json`, verify scripts, e2e hub lists, portfolio tests |
| **Catalog count drift** | Docs/tests still say “13 embeds” | Single source = `EMBED_GAMES.length` in registry; update contracts + ranking header in same PR |

### Legacy Equalize (single-file HTML) **[applicable if equalize bundle on host]**

Equalize ships as one self-contained `public/games/equalize/equalize.html` (not the TanStack CSR pipeline). Host-specific gates live on **dsapatterns-website**:

- **`window.EqualizeDebug`** from the canonical Equalize repo is intentional — upstream E2E depends on it. The host **minify plugin strips it** from `dist/`; **`verify-equalize-dist.mjs`** fails the build if it reappears in `dist/games/equalize/equalize.html`. Do not strip manually when syncing upstream unless the pipeline is broken.
- **Production minify** (`scripts/vite-plugin-minify-equalize.mjs`, registered in `vite.config.js`): after Vite copies `public/` → `dist/`, Terser runs on Equalize **inline** script (`compress`, **`mangle: true`**, **`drop_console: true`**, no comments) and **`levels.js`** (`mangle: false` so global **`LEVELS`** stays valid). No source maps for that step.
- **New games:** add parallel minify + verify only if shipping comparable inline debug hooks or one-liner `window` exports. TanStack suite uses Bharat embed build + `verify-game-dist-cloudflare.mjs` instead.

### Embed build pipeline (CSR in iframe)

- **`build-all-embeds.mjs`** orchestrates every slug in `EMBED_GAMES`: `DSAPATTERNS_EMBED=1` Vite build (`ssr: false`) → copy `.output/public` → `dist/client` → `patch-embed-client.mjs` (basepath, relative `./assets/`) → `generate-csr-index.mjs` (static `index.html` shell, no Nitro SSR fetch) → `patch-embed.mjs` (manifest / SW scope) → `vendor.mjs` rsync to `../dsapatterns-website/public/games/<slug>/`.
- **Never set `VITE_E2E` at build** — build script deletes it; auto-win is runtime `?e2e=1` only. Production no-auto-win e2e must hit **real** play/mode URLs without baking e2e into the bundle.
- Preview catalog: `node scripts/games/embed-preview-server.mjs` on port 5299; Playwright `baseURL` points there.
- **Upstream-first:** screenshot / bug from dsapatterns embeds or Android shells → fix in **Ranbhoomi / Bharat Brawlers** first, rebuild, then vendor. Do not patch only the host `public/games/` copy.
- **Deploy:** after vendoring, in dsapatterns-website run `npm test` (+ e2e as needed), commit `public/games/` + hub/SEO if catalog changed, push **`main` then FF-sync `master`** (`git merge --ff-only` — never force-overwrite). Cloudflare: git push alone may not refresh Workers — run `npm run build` + `wrangler versions upload` when Git integration is not the sole deploy path; purge CDN for `/` and `/games/*` if shells reference stale hashes.

