| Android SKUs for archived standalones | Ship **flagships** (TimeTwin / Circuit / GRID); do not publish `lumencircuit` / `orbitdefense` / `ghostloop` as new listings |

### Recent Learnings (July 2026)

- **Flagship mode consolidation (hard-delete standalones):** When two titles share a fantasy, **inline the secondary as `/modes/<name>`** under one flagship. **Learning**: (1) Keep mode source + unit tests. (2) Remove hub card, `public/games/<old>/`, embed + Android registry entries, SPA rewrite lists. (3) Add `LEGACY_GAME_SLUG_REDIRECTS` on **both** repos. (4) Retarget e2e/smoke/no-auto-win to mode URLs. (5) Challenge-relay payloads with `game: "lumen-circuit"` etc. must still resolve (storage keys / slug strings inside the mode may stay). Do **not** delete mode source because the hub card is gone.
- **Win celebrate vs `prefers-reduced-motion`:** If reduced-motion dwell equals (or is shorter than) the solve-hold before chrome mounts, the win overlay never paints and players think the game soft-locked. **Learning**: Split **hold** (keep solved board visible) from **celebrate visibility** (`CELEBRATE_VISIBLE_MS` ≥ ~2–4s even under reduced motion, or skip hold under reduced motion). Probe with `?celebrateProbe=1` / e2e asserting overlay ≥2s. Do not reintroduce confetti/`delayMs=4000` plans that fight the dwell/hold design.
- **Host shell height for mode lobbies:** Mode chrome + lobby CTAs need more vertical room than a bare canvas. **Learning**: Prefer ~**960px** floors / taller `clamp` on the host embed shell; verify Orbit/Lumen/Ghost mode home at 390×844 before calling mobile done.
- **Audio dock steals taps:** Shared mute/volume dock at top or mid-rail overlaps Modes / Play on short viewports. **Learning**: Equalize-style bottom-right chip + lobby bottom padding; pause overlays own their mute controls when present.
- **Catalog sync checklist:** One PR that changes the portfolio must touch registry, host `GamesSection` + SEO + routes, verify scripts, vercel/SPA slug lists, android registry + preview assertions, portfolio/registry contract tests, and ranking docs — or CI/host will disagree.
- **Dual-branch deploy hygiene:** After push to `main`, FF-sync `master` (`fetch` → `merge --ff-only`); never force-push over remote commits. Vendor script often pushes DSA `main` only — sync `master` in the same session.
- **Web Share API (`navigator.share`) vs Clipboard**: Silently falling back to `navigator.clipboard.writeText` when `navigator.share` fails or is unsupported (common on some desktop environments) creates a jarring UX. Users expect a native share sheet; getting a silent "Copied to clipboard" instead is confusing. **Learning**: Avoid silent fallbacks. If native share isn't reliably supported, either hide the share button entirely, or provide explicit, separate "Copy Link" and "Share" buttons so the user knows exactly what will happen.
- **Physics-Based CPU Opponents (Tank Wars)**: Implementing CPU AI in physics/trajectory games (like Tank Wars) doesn't require complex analytical math with wind integration. **Learning**: Use **Monte-Carlo simulation** during the CPU's turn. Run the deterministic physics loop headlessly 50-100 times with random angle/power variations, pick the trajectory that gets closest to the player, and add a small random `noise` variable to the final parameters so the CPU isn't unfairly perfect.
- **Embed auto-start when skipping tutorial levels**: Hiding the start overlay in embed (`isEmbedMode() && !isE2eMode()`) is not enough if the sim tick gates on `running === false` — users see a static canvas ("hung"). **Learning**: When embed auto-jumps to `START_LEVEL_INDEX > 0`, set `running = true` on mount in the same code path that hides the start screen. E2E must still use `?e2e=1` to begin at level 1 for `campaign-5`.
- **Progress epoch for start-level bumps**: Changing the first level players see invalidates old `localStorage` progress silently. **Learning**: Pair `START_LEVEL` / `START_LEVEL_INDEX` with a bumped `<slug>.progress_epoch`; on mismatch, reset progress to the new floor. Always exempt `?e2e=1` and document the epoch bump in the commit message.
- **Tower defense leak detection**: Checking only `pathIdx >= path.length` misses creeps that visually passed the exit column. **Learning**: Extract testable helpers (`leakExitX`, `creepHasLeaked`, tier-based `leakLifeCost`); treat leak when path is exhausted **or** creep center `x >= exit column`. Unit-test leak predicates separately from React.
- **TD win/lose same-frame race**: Clearing the last enemy and leaking on the same tick can show victory while lives hit zero. **Learning**: Mirror terminal flags in refs (`gameOverRef`, `wonRef`) read inside the RAF loop; stop `update()` when `gameOverRef` is true; on 0 lives set `won = false` explicitly — never infer defeat only from wave-clear logic.
- **Physics special ammo (Crush the Swappy)**: Players expect bombs to explode on **any** impact, not only when hitting a crush target. **Learning**: In Matter.js `collisionActive`/`collisionStart`, detonate when `ammoKind === "bomb"` on either body; keep crush scoring on separate target collisions.
- **Minimal embed copy beats briefing walls**: Long deploy/tutorial overlays shrink the playfield and do not improve retention. **Learning**: Steve-Jobs-style HUD — icon ammo bar, one-line goal, `⋯` for rare actions; invest juice in **damage feedback** (vignette, counters, near-miss signals) instead of more text.
- **Stable slug vs display rename**: Folder/display name can change (`Game Genesis Forge-2` → `Crush the Swappy`) without breaking bookmarks if **embed slug** (`crush-the-swappy`) stays fixed. **Learning**: `git mv` the folder; update `scripts/games/embed-registry.mjs`, e2e paths, capture-screenshots — do not rename `public/games/<slug>/` unless intentionally migrating URLs.
- **WinOverlay `testIdPrefix`**: Shared win overlay across games needs per-slug Playwright IDs without forking the component. **Learning**: Optional `testIdPrefix` prop → `{prefix}-win` / `{prefix}-continue`; pass slug-specific prefix from each game's play route.
- **Pure sim helpers in TD/puzzle cores**: Leak checks and solvers belong in `src/lib/` with `node --test` coverage, not buried in component effects — enables fast regression when tuning wave scripts or grid size.
- **TanStack route-tree build flake**: Occasional `Crawling result not available` during `routeTree.gen.ts` generation can fail `npm run build` for one game in `build-all-embeds.mjs`. **Learning**: Retry the single-game build; confirm new routes are imported in the router; do not vendor a partial dist to the host.
- **Difficulty budgets with flat penalties**: When calculating dynamic level difficulty budgets (e.g. scores or time), a purely multiplicative modifier (like 2x moves) mathematically breaks when the game has flat penalties (like a -500 score drop). Multiplicative budgets give long levels massive buffers while giving short levels zero margin for error. **Learning**: Use a **hybrid formula**: `(Cost * Multiplier) + Flat Armor`. The multiplier (e.g., `1.25x`) gives percentage leeway for wandering, and the `Flat Armor` (e.g., `+1000` points) ensures players can always absorb exactly N flat penalties on ANY level length. **Specific Example**: In Equalize, a "2x budget" gave a 4-move level only 120 points of buffer—meaning one undo (-300) resulted in game over. Changing the formula to `(optimalMoves * 30 * 1.25) + 1000` guaranteed every level had enough armor to survive exactly 2 illegal moves (-500 each).
- **Embed CSS vs touch:** Per-game `*-embed.css` can shrink shared chrome below 44px — audit computed size in the iframe, not source Tailwind alone.
- **Unused engine mechanics:** If filters/splitters/etc. already exist in the engine (Optic), ship levels that use them before inventing new systems or deleting the title.
- **Hub first emotion:** Registry `iframePath` / host iframeSrc should land on lobby or campaign first emotion — not buried rush/survival unless intentional.

